What this tool is

This memo is for a water system that wants to plan checks and replacements. The scores
help you decide where to look first. They are not an inspection. They are not a
legal finding. Reclassifying an unknown line as not lead must use a method the
Illinois EPA accepts.

{% if transfer_warning %}
How the scores were made

{{ transfer_warning }}

The Chicago model was trained on known customer-side rows in Chicago (snapshot
14 April 2025). It uses year built, the city's side of the pipe, nearby known lines,
and related fields. Many of those fields are missing in a small-system upload, so
the score is a rough transfer. Treat every unknown line as possibly lead until it
is checked.
{% else %}
How the scores were made

This run had {{ n_known }} known customer-side rows, which is at least 200, so a
new model was fit on this inventory only. The model predicts whether the property
side is lead or galvanized. It is calibrated on the same known rows, so the
percentages are a guide, not a proof. Treat every unknown line as possibly lead
until it is checked.
{% endif %}

A prediction never lowers urgency. "{{ treat_as_lead }}"

Verification sample

A fixed sample of {{ sample_n }} unknown lines was drawn. Strata are year-built
band and the city's side of the pipe. Sample size is not based on a margin of
error (that step is deferred). Use the sample to check lines, not to skip them.

Export

The CSV follows the Illinois EPA inventory template column order. Official
material columns are the recorded values (L, GRR, NL, U). Predicted probability
and confidence sit in extra columns. Do not copy a prediction into an official
class.

Limits

- One uploaded file, in memory only. Lead Line Lens does not store your inventory.
- Transfer from Chicago is unproven. Local field checks still decide the class.
- Small cells in public reports are suppressed; this private export lists every
  sampled line so a utility can go check it.
- This is not medical advice.

Sources: Illinois EPA lead service line inventory template; Lead Line Lens model
